./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:24:1272,Towards Applying Large Language Models to Complement Single-Cell Foundation Models,include_decision_unstable,EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|UNCERTAIN,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,wrapper_boundary,none,none,none,"scMPT fuses scGPT and LLM representations without generating text or conditioning on natural-language input; it applies existing LLMs as complementary, fitting application_wrapper exclusion.",EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,,,,,"The paper introduces scMPT, a fusion model that uses external LLM representations as side information to complement scGPT for single-cell analysis, fitting the application_wrapper exclusion. | The abstract describes scMPT as a fusion of scGPT and LLM representations for single-cell analysis, with no explicit generative mechanism; it is an application wrapper rather than a primary generative model.",EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,,,,,"The abstract describes scMPT as a fusion of scGPT and LLM representations for downstream single-cell tasks, with no natural-language text input/output or generative text-bio bridge, fitting the application wrapper exclusion. | The abstract presents scMPT as a fusion of scGPT and LLM representations, focusing on downstream task performance without describing a generative architecture or foundation-model characteristics; it is an application wrapper.",EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,,,,,"The paper introduces scMPT, a new model that fuses a single‑cell foundation model with LLM‑derived representations, establishing a substantive text‑bio multimodal bridge. | The abstract introduces scMPT, a model that fuses scGPT and LLM representations, but it does not mention any decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism. It references foundation models (scGPT, LLMs) but does not provide evidence that scMPT itself is a broadly pretrained foundation model.",UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,none,"leverages synergies between scGPT, and single-cell representations from LLMs that capture these insights",none,"The abstract presents scMPT, a new model that fuses scGPT with LLM‑derived representations, indicating a bridge between text‑trained models and single‑cell data, but it does not explicitly describe natural‑language text input or generation, leaving the text component status uncertain.",thin_or_truncated_abstract;wrapper_boundary;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:25:3178,VCWorld: A Biological World Model for Virtual Cell Simulation,include_decision_unstable,EXCLUDE|UNCERTAIN|UNCERTAIN|INCLUDE|INCLUDE,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,clear_exclude,none,none,cell-level white-box simulator,"VCWorld is a simulator that predicts cellular responses using LLM reasoning, but lacks natural-language text input/output and explicit generative mechanism, so text_component=no and generative=no, leading to exclusion.",UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,none,none,"generates interpretable, stepwise predictions","The abstract presents VCWorld as a new model integrating LLM reasoning for virtual cell simulation, but does not explicitly describe natural-language text input/output or a generative mechanism, leaving text component and generative status unclear. Thus, it is a thin abstract boundary case.",UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,none,none,generates interpretable stepwise predictions,"Abstract describes a cell simulator using LLM reasoning but does not explicitly mention natural-language text input/output or a generative architecture; text component and text-bio bridge are unclear, and generative status is unclear due to lack of explicit generative mechanism.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract introduces VCWorld as a new model that combines biological data (gene expression, perturbations) with large language model reasoning, providing clear evidence of both a biological modality and a substantive text component forming a text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents VCWorld as a new model that ""generates interpretable, stepwise predictions"" using the reasoning capabilities of large language models, indicating a generative architecture, and it explicitly leverages LLMs, providing foundation‑model evidence.",INCLUDE,,,clear_include,"generates interpretable, stepwise predictions",integrates structured biological knowledge with the iterative reasoning capabilities of large language models,large language models,"The abstract describes VCWorld as a new model that combines structured biological knowledge with large language model reasoning to generate stepwise textual predictions, providing a clear text‑bio bridge and using a generative LLM component; therefore it meets all inclusion criteria.",thin_or_truncated_abstract;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:26:181,scOTM: A Deep Learning Framework for Predicting Single-Cell Perturbation Responses with Large Language Models.,include_decision_unstable,EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|INCLUDE|INCLUDE,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,,,,,"scOTM uses LLM-derived embeddings as prior biological knowledge for predicting transcriptional responses, but does not incorporate natural-language text as input or output, nor does it present a multimodal text-bio generative model; it is an application wrapper. | scOTM uses a variational autoencoder (generative) to predict single-cell perturbation responses, but it is a specialized prediction model without broad pretraining or foundation-model characteristics.",EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,wrapper_boundary,none,none,variational autoencoder,"The abstract presents a VAE that uses LLM-derived representations as prior biological knowledge for predicting perturbation responses, but no natural-language text component or text-bio alignment is central; thus it is an application wrapper, not a primary generative text-bio model.",EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,wrapper_boundary,none,none,variational autoencoder,"scOTM uses LLM-derived representations as input features for a VAE predicting perturbation responses, with no natural-language text or text-bio bridge; this is a wrapper use of an external LLM for a downstream predictor, not a central multimodal text-bio model.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract presents scOTM as a new deep‑learning framework (primary model) that predicts single‑cell perturbation responses using LLM‑derived representations, providing a clear natural‑language text component and a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents scOTM, a VAE‑based framework that predicts whole‑transcriptome perturbation responses (generative) and incorporates representations from large language models (foundation model evidence).",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract introduces scOTM as a new deep learning framework that predicts single‑cell perturbation responses using LLM‑derived representations, establishing both a biological modality (single‑cell transcriptomics) and a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents scOTM, a VAE-based framework that predicts whole-transcriptome responses and leverages embeddings from large language models, evidencing a generative architecture and foundation-model characteristics.",wrapper_boundary;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary
