./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:31:1818,CaLMFlow: Volterra Flow Matching using Causal Language Models,stable_include,UNCERTAIN|INCLUDE|UNCERTAIN|INCLUDE|INCLUDE,UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,text_component_boundary,none,none,continuous data generation; flow matching,"Abstract presents a novel flow matching framework using LLMs for continuous data generation, with application to single-cell perturbation. Text component and text-bio bridge are unclear because the abstract only mentions 'textual context' without explicit natural-language input/output or alignment. Generative model is clear.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"CaLMFlow is a primary model paper that uses causal language models for flow matching, applied to single-cell perturbation response prediction with textual context, satisfying all criteria. | Introduces CaLMFlow, a flow matching framework using causal language models for continuous data generation, demonstrated on single-cell perturbation response prediction, indicating a generative text-bio model.",UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,incorporate textual context,incorporate textual context for single-cell perturbation response prediction,flow matching for continuous data generation,"CaLMFlow is a primary model paper presenting a flow matching framework using LLMs for continuous data generation, with single-cell perturbation response prediction. However, the abstract does not clearly describe a natural-language text component or explicit text-bio alignment; both text_component and text_bio_bridge remain unclear. Scope reviewer flagged these as unclear, while architecture reviewer did not address them.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract presents a new framework (CaLMFlow) using LLMs and explicitly mentions applying it to single‑cell perturbation response prediction, indicating a biological modality, a substantive text component, and a text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents CaLMFlow, a novel framework that leverages large language models for continuous data generation via flow matching, indicating a primary generative model with foundation-model characteristics.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The paper introduces a novel LLM‑based flow‑matching model applied to single‑cell data and explicitly mentions using textual context, indicating a substantive text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents CaLMFlow, a novel framework that uses large language models to perform flow matching and generate continuous data, indicating a genuine generative architecture and leveraging a foundation model.",thin_or_truncated_abstract;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary
